    {
      "id": 1775785905884,
      "rule": "PREFER: pools where winning top LPers show feePercent materially above losers; in both Tortellini-SOL and milkers-SOL, winners captured roughly 18-54% fees while loser cohorts were mostly ~15-19%, so strong fee capture is a better signal than raw hold time alone.",
      "tags": [
        "top-lpers",
        "fees",
        "cross-pool"
      ],
      "outcome": "manual",
      "sourceType": "manual",
      "pinned": false,
      "role": "GENERAL",
      "created_at": "2026-04-10T01:51:45.884Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 1775785913112,
      "rule": "PREFER: mixed hold-duration pools over pure scalper assumptions. Tortellini-SOL had profitable top LPers at about 0.8h, 3.8h, and 9.9h holds, while milkers-SOL had winners from about 0.1h scalp trades up to 28-32h holds; profitable behavior can span both short and long holds when ranges are well placed.",
      "tags": [],
      "outcome": "manual",
      "sourceType": "manual",
      "pinned": false,
      "role": "GENERAL",
      "created_at": "2026-04-10T01:51:53.112Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 1775785920798,
      "rule": "PREFER: adapting style to pool character. Tortellini-SOL top historical winners leaned medium-width ranges with both spot and bid_ask working, while milkers-SOL showed its best durable winners using tight bid_ask or medium spot placements; avoid one-style-fits-all assumptions across pools.",
      "tags": [
        "top-lpers",
        "range-style",
        "strategy"
      ],
      "outcome": "manual",
      "sourceType": "manual",
      "pinned": false,
      "role": "GENERAL",
      "created_at": "2026-04-10T01:52:00.798Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 1775786022555,
      "rule": "PREFER: pools where winning top LPers show materially higher feePercent than losing cohorts; across Tortellini, milkers, and BULL, winners generally captured much stronger fee share than weaker cohorts, so prioritize pools/ranges that convert time in range into superior fee capture rather than judging hold time alone.",
      "tags": [
        "top-lpers",
        "fee-capture",
        "cross-pool"
      ],
      "outcome": "manual",
      "sourceType": "manual",
      "pinned": false,
      "role": "GENERAL",
      "created_at": "2026-04-10T01:53:42.555Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 1775786033750,
      "rule": "PREFER: mixed hold-duration pools over a pure scalper-only model. Across Tortellini, BULL, and milkers, profitable LPs appeared from sub-1h trades up through multi-hour and multi-day holds, so do not reject a pool only because winners are not all fast scalpers.",
      "tags": [
        "top-lpers",
        "hold-time",
        "cross-pool"
      ],
      "outcome": "manual",
