    },
    {
      "id": 1775786044411,
      "rule": "PREFER: medium-width ranges as the default starting shape when top-LPer evidence is mixed. Tortellini, GHOST, and BULL all showed top winners clustering around medium widths, while very tight ranges only stood out as a pool-specific edge in milkers.",
      "tags": [
        "range",
        "top-lpers",
        "cross-pool"
      ],
      "outcome": "manual",
      "sourceType": "manual",
      "pinned": false,
      "role": "GENERAL",
      "created_at": "2026-04-10T01:54:04.411Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 1775786050229,
      "rule": "PREFER: treating milkers-like pools as a special case. Unlike Tortellini, GHOST, and BULL, milkers showed both durable 28-32h winners and ultra-short sub-0.5h scalps succeeding with tight ranges and very high feePercent, so this pool can reward both disciplined scalping and longer holds when fee capture stays exceptionally strong.",
      "tags": [],
      "outcome": "manual",
      "sourceType": "manual",
      "pinned": false,
      "role": "GENERAL",
      "created_at": "2026-04-10T01:54:10.229Z"
    },
    {
      "id": 1775792226141,
      "rule": "PREFER: GENZ-SOL-type pools where top LP winners are short-duration operators; across two GENZ pools, the strongest winners mostly held about 0.15h to 2.6h, so treat GENZ as a fast-turnover pool and do not assume long passive holds are the edge.",
